course: dictionary
lesson: 8438
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word saddle can be a thing (a noun) or an action (a verb). «The rider put the saddle on the horse's back.» Here saddle is a thing: a leather seat.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «The cowboys saddled their horses before dawn», saddled is a verb: they put saddles on the horses. The -ed ending tells you it happened in the past.
explain: Some phrases use saddle in a new way. «She was saddled with the washing-up all week» is not about a seat at all. Saddled with means given a hard job that nobody wants. If the basic meaning does not fit the sentence, look for a different meaning.
fact: A saddle is a leather seat put on a horse's back for the rider.
fact: The seat of a bicycle or motorbike is also called a saddle.
fact: To saddle a horse means to put a saddle on it.
fact: «Saddle someone with» means to give them a hard job they don't want.
fact: The shells of Galápagos giant tortoises can be saddle-shaped, which helps them stretch up to tall cactus.
exercise: «The rider put the saddle on the horse's back.» In this sentence, what is a saddle? | A stable where horses sleep | *A leather seat for the rider | A rope for tying up the horse | A bag of hay
exercise: «She was saddled with the washing-up all week.» What does saddled with mean? | Given a shiny new bicycle | *Given a hard job nobody wanted | Sat on a horse with a rope | Asked to go swimming
exercise: «Mia raised the saddle on her bike so her legs could stretch.» What is the saddle? | A bell | *The seat of a bicycle | A brake | A pedal
test: «The cowboy will saddle the horse at dawn.» What kind of word is saddle here? | *A verb: putting a saddle on | A noun: a seat | A noun: a rope | A verb: running away
test: «Saddle up, team, we ride at noon!» What does saddle up mean? | *Get ready and put the saddles on the horses | Go swimming in the river | Fall asleep in the sun | Hide behind a rock
exam: «On Monday morning the Horse came first, "with a saddle on his back and a bit in his mouth".» What does saddle mean here? | A type of shoe | A tall tree | A bag for carrying books | *A leather seat for a rider
